.nh
.TH "PB-CONFIG-SYNC" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-config-sync - Validate and apply this machine's configuration file


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb config sync [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Validate and apply this machine's configuration file

.PP
Inspect, initialize, validate, or apply this machine's authoritative configuration file. The file defines repository choices and explicit path rules. Validate the effective configuration before applying a confirmed change to the enrolled machine's synchronization assignment.

.PP
Configuration commands distinguish local CLI settings from synchronized repository content. Inspect current state before changing it; synchronization reports conflicts instead of silently overwriting one side. The --json option provides structured output for scripts where supported.

.PP
With --json, this command group lists its available commands.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for sync


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-config(1)\fP, \fBpb-config-sync-apply(1)\fP, \fBpb-config-sync-init(1)\fP, \fBpb-config-sync-path(1)\fP, \fBpb-config-sync-validate(1)\fP
